###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training on a single core of an Intel Xeon Gold 6271 CPU (128 GB RAM):
# at the full data set about 210 min for AENET at 300 epochs and about 460
# min for MTP; AENET at 3,300 epochs about 38 h (Figs. 4, 5).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - AENET uses Chebyshev-expanded radial and angular distribution functions, not Behler-Parrinello symmetry functions; recorded under the new registry method ChebyshevANN (decision on its name and scope wanted).
# - Test RMSEs at the full data-set size are read from the numbers printed in the Fig. 3 heat map (upper triangles); training RMSEs are stated in the text. The text gives MTP/SNAP force training errors as 0.22-0.24 eV/A while Fig. 3 prints 0.25 and 0.26, so they are not encoded.
# - Hyperparameters are in Table S1 (SI), not encoded. qSNAP was trained only on small subsets and dropped.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/choyal2024.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

